From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Use the constrained high profile when it gives a better mode

A receiver lists the modes it decodes per H.264 profile, and a television
can take 1080p at 60 Hz in the constrained high profile while its
constrained baseline entry stops at 30 Hz. The client always chose the
baseline entry ("XXX: Pick the better profile if we have an encoder that
supports it!"), and logged only that entry's modes, so a 60 Hz full HD mode
was never used or even seen.

wfd_client_choose_codec() now picks between the entries. Baseline stays in
use unless an entry the encoder can produce shows the source better: more of
it, or the same at a higher refresh rate. x264 and the VA encoders produce
the high profile; only OpenH264 is limited to baseline. Every entry the
receiver offers is logged, with its profile and level.

With the high profile x264 now uses the tools that make it compress better
than baseline at the same bitrate, CABAC and the 8x8 transform. The bitrate
limit grows with the refresh rate, so a 60 Hz frame gets as many bits as a
30 Hz one, within the receiver's announced maximum.

